<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP copper output soars in October.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP copper output soars in October.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd said on Tuesday that copper output from its Escondida mine in Chile and the Magma Copper operations rose in the month of October but Papua New Guinea production fell.</p>
<p>The company, the world's second largest coppper producer, also said in it monthly production report that PNG shipments were also lower due to unfavourable weather conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;Production of both copper in concentrate and copper cathodes was higher for October compared to the same month last year reflecting the acquisition of Magma and the Phase Three expansion of the Escondida mine in Chile,&quot; BHP said.  </p>
<p>&quot;These factors were also reflected in higher shipments of copper in concentrate,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Total copper in concentrate production rose 49 percent to 59,700 tonnes in October and rose by 37 percent in the first five months of 1996/97 (June/May) to 297,200 tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;Production in Papua New Guinea was lower for the first months to October compared to the same period last year as a result of lower mill throughput and lower recoveries,&quot; BHP said.  </p>
